WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.862
One rule needs a closer look,
because the sources don't line up.

2
00:00:03.862 --> 00:00:06.991
Learn says report-only
policies don't block anyone,

3
00:00:06.991 --> 00:00:09.599
so they don't need the
emergency exclusion.

4
00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:15.034
Book 04's pre-merge check is stricter,
and fails any report-only file without it,

5
00:00:15.034 --> 00:00:18.175
even the probe that's
meant to exclude nobody.

6
00:00:18.175 --> 00:00:22.575
The chapter's finding is that the
stricter rule isn't wrong, just stricter.

7
00:00:22.575 --> 00:00:26.629
So the code puts the exclusion in
every file whatever its state,

8
00:00:26.629 --> 00:00:29.825
because enforcing a file
means changing one word.

9
00:00:29.825 --> 00:00:32.836
Only a named report-only
instrument may skip it,

10
00:00:32.836 --> 00:00:35.590
and it fails the moment
someone enables it.
